The '''Boreal Islands''' ({{Langx|bl|Illas de Boreal}}), or simply '''the Boreals''' (''Las Boreales''), are an {{W|archipelago}} in the [[Northern Ocean]], located on the [[Arktici Shelf|Arktici Continental Shelf]]. The principal islands are about {{cvt|480|km|mi}} from the southern tip of [[Cerdanya]], and about {{convert|1210|km|mi}} from the [[W:Cape Dubouzet|southern tip]] of the [[Arktici Peninsula]].

The archipelago has a substantial degree of internal {{W|self-governance}}, and the territory is a {{W|demilitarized zone}}.

In the past, despite their geographic isolation, the Boreals played an important role in geopolitical dynamics during the [[Colonial history of Lurando-Abyala|colonial era]] following the [[Great Disappointment]]. The presence of the [[Ryuji Takemoto]] and his colonists in [[Cerdanya|western Cerdanya]] had spooked colonial authorities, who sought to accelerate their settlement of the territory. At the same time, Volisanian authority in the [[Northern Triangle]] [[Volisanya Boba|was minimal]], and near nonexistent in the Arktic region. As the [[United Kingdoms of Volisania|United Kingdoms]] descended into [[Volisanian Civil War|civil war]] the [[Commonwealth of Cerdanya]] began to exercise authority over the [[Sea of Shuainia]] and the wider [[Northern Ocean]], and cultivated closer trade relations with the [[Fosian colonization of Lurando-Abyala|Fosian colonies]] and the [[Fosia|Fosian mainland]] in an attempt to minimize the disruption caused by the collapse of trade with the Volisanian metropole.  

=== Baliscan visa policy ===
In 1949, the Baliscan government designated the Boreals as an entirely visa-free zone, adopting the policy known as {{W|free migration}}. Before this the 1738 [[Treaty of Rosari]] between the [[Commonwealth of Cerdanya]] and the [[State of Zong]] granted Zong (and their tributary states) equal right of abode as Baliscan nationals in the territory. Non-treaty nationals may live and work indefinitely visa-free as well. "Regulations concerning rejection and expulsion from the Sant Pere " is in force on non-discriminatory basis. However, travelers who have a visa requirement to enter mainland Balisca must have a [[Baliscan Visa Protocol|Visa Protocol]]-compliant visa if they travel via mainland Balisca. This must be a double-entry visa so they can return to mainland Balisca.

Those traveling to and from the Boreals outside of the [[Abyalan Mutual Development Community]] must bring {{W|passports}} or {{W|national identity cards}}, as all are subject to identity check. Passports or national identity cards satisfy the Conosur regulatory requirements for identity verification. Due to a transitional arrangement, Baliscan citizens can also prove their identity with a document issued in Balisca which include at least name, photo and date of birth, such as a Baliscan driving license issued after 1998; the transitional period ends on 31 August 2022.

